sequenceDiagram
    accTitle: Browser login and department authorization
    accDescr: The browser authenticates with local Keycloak and LDAP. Airflow exchanges the authorization code over verified TLS, synchronizes group-based roles, and applies department permissions to UI and API requests.
    autonumber
    participant B as Local browser
    participant T as Traefik ingress
    participant A as Airflow API / FAB
    participant K as Keycloak
    participant L as OpenLDAP
    participant P as PostgreSQL

    B->>T: HTTPS https://localhost
    T->>A: HTTP :8080
    A-->>B: Redirect to Keycloak authorization endpoint
    B->>K: HTTPS https://localhost:8443 + login form
    K->>L: LDAP credential check and group lookup
    L-->>K: User identity and department groups
    K->>P: Identity and session persistence in keycloak database
    K-->>B: Redirect with authorization code + state
    B->>T: HTTPS /auth/oauth-authorized/keycloak
    T->>A: Forward callback
    A->>K: Verified TLS to internal Keycloak service: token exchange + userinfo
    K-->>A: Identity and group claims
    A->>P: Sync FAB roles at login and persist session in airflow database
    A-->>B: Authenticated session / JWT cookie
    B->>T: Request department DAG via UI or REST API
    T->>A: Forward authenticated request
    A->>P: Resolve role and DAG-specific permissions
    A-->>B: Authorized result or access denial
    Note over A,P: Example: aid-finance-auth can access the finance DAG. Other departments are denied by the API.
    Note over B,L: TLS protects browser and OIDC traffic. The local LDAP connection is inside the trusted Docker network.
